Usage: cmp [OPTION]... FILE1 [FILE2 [SKIP1 [SKIP2]]]

Compare two files byte by byte.

Compare FILE1 with FILE2.
If FILE1 or FILE2 is -, read standard input.

Exit status is 0 if inputs are the same, 1 if different, 2 if trouble.

FILE1 FILE2 may be followed by SKIP1 and SKIP2 for GNU-compatible
initial byte skipping.

OPTIONS:
  -b, --print-bytes         print differing bytes
  -i, --ignore-initial ARG  skip specified number of initial bytes
  -l, --verbose             output byte numbers of differing bytes
  -n, --bytes ARG           compare specified number of bytes
  -s, --quiet               silent mode
      --help                display this help and exit
  -V, --version             output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
